}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.3 The parse cost moved to the workers}

\p{All proofs of the export decoded once into worker overlays (\code{\verb~|Overlay.blockRoot(block)~} against \code{\verb~|RangeDecoder.decode(range)~}, \code{\verb~|resetTo~} after each), by 8 threads taking runs of 32 in file order; CPU time summed over the threads (\code{\verb~|ThreadMXBean~}). "Without foreign" = the same run with every foreign reference answered by a constant; "tokenise" = the bytes of all ranges through the template scanner, nothing built, one thread.}

\table{
\tr{\th{}\th{Init}\th{Std}\th{cedar}\th{mathlib}}
\tr{\td{proofs decoded, blocks / ranges}\td{37,600 / 37,447}\td{64,516 / 64,250}\td{73,305 / 72,351}\td{475,131 / 473,119}}
\tr{\td{overlay nodes, from blocks}\td{5,071,208}\td{7,808,269}\td{11,352,346}\td{78,207,170}}
\tr{\td{overlay nodes, from ranges (of which foreign)}\td{6,000,156 (964,561 = 16.1 \%)}\td{9,597,147 (1,848,246 = 19.3 \%)}\td{14,695,526 (3,421,144 = 23.3 \%)}\td{92,748,947 (15,334,165 = 16.5 \%)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{CPU, 8 workers, from blocks}}\td{\strong{0.159 s} (31.3 ns / node, 4.2 us / proof)}\td{\strong{0.230 s} (29.4 ns / node, 3.6 us / proof)}\td{\strong{0.313 s} (27.6 ns / node, 4.3 us / proof)}\td{\strong{2.653 s} (33.9 ns / node, 5.6 us / proof)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{CPU, 8 workers, from ranges}}\td{\strong{0.512 s} (85.4 ns / node, 13.7 us / proof)}\td{\strong{0.921 s} (96.0 ns / node, 14.3 us / proof)}\td{\strong{1.648 s} (112.2 ns / node, 22.8 us / proof)}\td{\strong{9.583 s} (103.3 ns / node, 20.3 us / proof)}}
\tr{\td{moved to the workers (ranges minus blocks)}\td{+0.354 s (x 3.2)}\td{+0.692 s (x 4.0)}\td{+1.335 s (x 5.3)}\td{+6.930 s (x 3.6)}}
\tr{\td{- from ranges, without foreign records}\td{0.243 s (x 1.5)}\td{0.404 s (x 1.8)}\td{0.570 s (x 1.8)}\td{4.841 s (x 1.8)}}
\tr{\td{- the foreign records}\td{0.269 s (279 ns each, 53 \% of the decode)}\td{0.517 s (280 ns each, 56 \% of the decode)}\td{1.079 s (315 ns each, 65 \% of the decode)}\td{4.742 s (309 ns each, 49 \% of the decode)}}
\tr{\td{- tokenising the ranges alone (1 thread)}\td{0.152 s (1753 MB/s, 30.3 ns / record)}\td{0.245 s (1716 MB/s, 31.7 ns / record)}\td{0.340 s (1895 MB/s, 30.1 ns / record)}\td{2.137 s (2033 MB/s, 27.6 ns / record)}}
\tr{\td{foreign: requests / range lookups / probes per search / lines walked}\td{342,576 / 427,172 / 1.02 / 2,336,900}\td{538,550 / 713,396 / 1.03 / 4,407,524}\td{799,235 / 1,061,899 / 1.07 / 8,690,629}\td{3,752,961 / 4,809,926 / 1.02 / 36,637,804}}
\tr{\td{CPU, 1 worker, blocks -> ranges}\td{0.168 -> 0.560 s}\td{0.243 -> 0.986 s}\td{0.322 -> 1.554 s}\td{not run}}
\tr{\td{wall clock, 8 workers, blocks -> ranges}\td{0.023 -> 0.067 s}\td{0.036 -> 0.126 s}\td{0.046 -> 0.270 s}\td{0.338 -> 1.397 s}}
}

\p{Reading: the worker's own range costs 1.5 - 1.8 times the block decode (28 - 32 ns of tokenising per record on top of 20 - 35 ns for the node and its location reads; text is 53 - 56 bytes per record, a block record 4.4 - 4.7). The foreign records cost as much again or more: 16 - 23 \% more nodes at 280 - 315 ns each. One worker and eight workers spend about the same CPU time (cedar: 6 \% more with eight); the file pages were in the page cache.}
}

